    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **65 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors**, BUILD SUCCESS.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the structured audit event in `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`, emitted via the dedicated `AUDIT` logger alongside the existing human-readable audit line.\n\n**What was added** (`src/main/java/.../rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`):\n\n- **`CREATE_SEQUENCE`** \u2014 a static `AtomicInteger` giving each event a monotonically increasing `seq` across all creates for the application's lifetime.\n- **`OwnerCreatedEvent`** \u2014 an immutable Java `record` whose component order (`seq`, `ownerId`, `customerCode`, `membershipLevel`, `event`) is exactly the JSON field order, serialized with a Jackson `ObjectMapper`.\n- **`emitOwnerCreatedEvent(owner)`** \u2014 builds and logs the event as JSON, e.g. `{\"seq\":1,\"ownerId\":11,\"customerCode\":\"NSW-16E6609E\",\"membershipLevel\":1,\"event\":\"OWNER_CREATED\"}`.\n- **`primaryIdentifier(owner)`** \u2014 returns the owner's current primary identifier (the customer code today). This is the single seam the spec calls out: when the customer code is later unified into a member id, only this method changes and the event automatically carries the member id, since the event reads the identifier through it rather than pulling `customerCode` directly.\n\nThe new event line is additive, so existing audit assertions (e.g. Cp21's line check) still pass, and Cp53's new assertion \u2014 that one `AUDIT` event contains `OWNER_CREATED`, the owner id, and the customer code \u2014 is satisfied.",
